export anchor MidCenturyModernStyle:
    number: 61
    screen: Calendar
    name: Mid-century modern
    idea: A 1950s hi-fi console of a calendar, with walnut, mustard and teal, starbursts and boomerangs, and each day as a long rounded lane along an hour dial.
    base: light
    palette:
        cream: #f4ecd8, the page
        card: #fffaf0, day lanes, the console band and the style sheet
        walnut: #5a3a22, the top bar, borders, the view switch and the console ledge
        teal: #1d6b67, the primary button, event duration bars and the today lane border
        tealTint: #cfe6e1, the current week row in the month
        mustard: #e2a72e, the selected nav item and view, the starburst and the focus outline
        mustardTint: #f8e4b5, deadline chips
        tomato: #b4432a, deadline chip borders and the starburst key
        ink: #2a2118, text
        muted: #6b5a48, labels, times and the hour ruler
    type:
        Rounded geometric sans throughout, Futura, Century Gothic, Avenir
        Next, URW Gothic, Trebuchet MS, sans-serif. Sizes are 32px bold for the
        week title, 34px bold day numbers, 13px bold uppercase labels with
        0.2em tracking, 14px bold event titles and 13px body. Nav and view
        labels are uppercase with wide tracking.
    layout:
        A walnut top bar with a mustard and teal starburst mark, the spaced
        uppercase wordmark, pill nav with the current item in mustard and a
        boomerang outline drifting off the right edge. Below come the week
        title and the controls. The side panel becomes a console band across
        the page in three parts, the month table, the calendar checkboxes as
        cream pills, and an away card for Lena with a boomerang medallion. The
        week is seven horizontal lanes, a 150px day label on the left and a
        lane marked every hour from 09 to 17 hours under a shared ruler. All
        day items are chips at the top of a lane. Each timed event is a teal
        bar exactly as long as the event, with its time, title and people
        beneath, aligned right for late events. Below 760px the console stacks
        and each lane becomes a plain list with short bars as bullets.
    spacing: An 8px unit. 10px between lanes, 18 to 24px inside panels and 32px between areas.
    density: Medium. One lane per day about 104px tall.
    corners: Full pills for controls and chips. Lanes alternate 18px and 60px corners like a boomerang, event bars use 12px and 2px.
    borders: 2px walnut on secondary buttons, fields and the console, dotted 2px tan dividers inside the console. Deadline chips have a 2px tomato border and out of office chips a 2px dashed walnut border.
    shadows: Hard offsets only. A 4px mustard offset under the primary button and a walnut ledge under the console.
    icons:
        Solid filled shapes at text size. A dot marks Team, a four point
        starburst marks Deadline and a boomerang marks Out of office, each
        with its word. Today in the month is a mustard starburst.
    focus: A 3px mustard outline offset 2px with a 6px dark walnut halo.
    tone: Breezy and period, such as The week ahead, Calendars on air and Nothing on the dial.
